{"compatibility":"as-is","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: as-is.

Protected data: none. `N1` and `N2` are context inputs used only as array sizes for generated quantities; they are not observed/scored by the model.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

No changes were required. The program contains no model-block likelihood or parameter priors, no protected observations, and no forbidden manual log-density manipulation.
","model_safe_stan":"data {
  int<lower=1> N1;
  int<lower=1> N2;
}

transformed data {
  real<lower=0> A = 3;
  real phi = 4;

  real<lower=0> omega1 = 2;
  real<lower=0> alpha1 = 3;
  real<lower=0> beta1 = 0.25;

  real<lower=0> omega2 = 1;
  real<lower=0> alpha2 = 38;
  real<lower=0> beta2 = 4.5;

  real gamma = 0.5;
  real sigma = 0.5;
}

generated quantities {
  array[N1] real x1;
  array[N1] real y1;

  array[N2] real x2;
  array[N2] real y2;

  for (n in 1:N1) {
    x1[n] = gamma_rng(alpha1, beta1 + gamma * omega1);
    y1[n] = normal_rng(A * sin(omega1 * x1[n] + phi), sigma);
  }

  for (n in 1:N2) {
    x2[n] = gamma_rng(alpha2, beta2 + gamma * omega2);
    y2[n] = normal_rng(A * sin(omega2 * x2[n] + phi), sigma);
  }
}

","data_safe_json":"{
  "N1": 4,
  "N2": 5
}","protected_variables":[]}
